@startuml
title One struct, two encodings: the ABI must be intrinsic, the storage may be packed
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}

rectangle "Caller\nTypeScript client or another contract\nencodes arguments in Noir's intrinsic layout" as Caller
rectangle "struct CreditEvents {\n  flag_default: bool,\n  flag_redeemed: bool,\n  rating: FieldCompressedString,\n}" as S
rectangle "Serialize / Deserialize (derived)\n[flag_default, flag_redeemed, rating]\n3 Fields, fixed by the ABI" as Ser
rectangle "Packable (hand-written)\n[flags bits, rating]\n2 Fields, internal to the contract" as Pack
rectangle "Public storage\nPublicMutable<CreditEvents>\n2 slots: 2 SLOAD / 2 SSTORE" as Store
rectangle "Return value / event\n[Field; 3]" as Ret

Caller --> Ser : arguments
Ser --> S : Deserialize
S --> Pack : write(x) calls pack()
Pack --> Store
Store --> Pack : read() calls unpack()
Pack --> S
S --> Ser : serialize()
Ser --> Ret

note right of Ser
  Hand-rolling this one compiles and then
  fails every call: "arguments hash mismatch".
end note
note right of Pack
  Only obligation: unpack(pack(x)) == x.
  Changing N moves every slot declared
  after the variable in #[storage].
end note
@enduml
